Version 0.1.2
-------------
    * On a Mac, the toolchain's cc and c++ drop -static for the Mac's own
      binaries, which macOS cannot link statically. go-rules' DefaultStatic
      can then stay on for a Mac: an architecture subrepo takes it from the
      host's config, so turning it off on a Mac also left ///linux_* Go
      binaries with only the standard library's cgo unlinkable.

Version 0.1.1
-------------
    * please_zig zon: a package's deps are the targets of the hashes it
      depends on, not the names it declared them by, so two versions of one
      package each reach their own dependents. Targets are given in order of
      name then hash, so the output no longer depends on fetch order.

Version 0.1.0
-------------
    * First release: zig_library, zig_binary, zig_test, zig_static_library,
      zig_shared_library, zig_c_library and zig_package, with please_zig
      zon to write package rules from a build.zig.zon. A C toolchain over
      zig (:toolchain) that cross-compiles for other plugins to use. Zig
      0.17.0.
